cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SimpleFWI, cite this software and record the exact commit,
  configuration, and data provenance used in your experiment.
type: software
title: "SimpleFWI: 2D Full-Waveform Inversion in PyTorch"
authors:
  - family-names: Izzatullah
    given-names: Muhammad
repository-code: https://github.com/izzatum/SimpleFWI
url: https://github.com/izzatum/SimpleFWI
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  SimpleFWI is a Python research library for two-dimensional,
  constant-density acoustic full-waveform inversion in the frequency domain.
  Its PyTorch API includes a Helmholtz solver with perfectly matched layers
  and an optional free surface, multi-resolution and multi-frequency
  continuation, native PyTorch optimizers, implicit adjoint gradients, and
  matrix-free exact and Gauss-Newton Hessian-vector products for local
  uncertainty studies. CPU sparse-direct solves provide the reference path;
  experimental CUDA solves have been validated on small numerical examples.
keywords:
  - full-waveform inversion
  - PyTorch
  - 2D acoustic modeling
  - frequency-domain inversion
  - Helmholtz equation
  - perfectly matched layer
  - seismic inversion
  - geophysics
  - multi-frequency continuation
  - Hessian-vector products
